<title>USA: U.S. propane stocks fall 2.2 million bbls in week.</title>
<headline>U.S. propane stocks fall 2.2 million bbls in week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. propane stocks fell 2.2 million barrels in the week ending February 14 to below the normal range for the first time since December 1996, the Energy Information Administration report on Thursday showed.</p>
<p>The EIA report said total stocks were at 27.7 million barrels, with most of the draw in the U.S. Gulf Coast.</p>
<p>The Gulf Coast showed a 1.6 million barrel draw, while the Midwest had a 400,000 barrel drawdown. The East Coast was unchanged.</p>
